    {
        "url": "https://docs.langchain.com/.well-known/agent-skills/langchain/skill.md",
        "domain": "docs.langchain.com",
        "endpoint": "/.well-known/agent-skills/langchain/skill.md",
        "filename": "skill.md",
        "content": "---\nname: langchain\ndescription: Use when building AI agents with tool calling, managing agent workflows, configuring models and tools, adding middleware for custom behavior, testing and evaluating agents, or deploying to production. Covers LangChain (agent framework), LangGraph (orchestration runtime), and Deep Agents (batteries-included harness).\nmetadata:\n    mintlify-proj: langchain\n    version: \"1.0\"\n---\n\n# LangChain Skill\n\n## Product summary\n\nLangChain is an open-source framework for building AI agents and applications. It provides three complementary layers: **LangChain** (agent framework with models, tools, and middleware), **LangGraph** (low-level orchestration runtime for stateful workflows), and **Deep Agents** (batteries-included harness with filesystem, memory, subagents, and planning). Use `create_agent()` for a configurable agent harness, `StateGraph` for custom workflows, or `create_deep_agent()` for complex tasks with built-in capabilities. Agents are built on top of LangGraph and automatically support tracing through LangSmith. Primary docs: https://docs.langchain.com\n\n**Key files and commands:**\n- `create_agent()` – Create a basic agent with model, tools, and system prompt\n- `create_deep_agent()` – Create an agent with filesystem, memory, subagents, and planning\n- `StateGraph` – Define custom agent workflows as nodes and edges\n- Middleware – Customize agent behavior with hooks (wrap_model_call, wrap_tool_call, before_model, after_model)\n- `invoke()` – Run an agent with messages and optional thread_id for persistence\n- `stream()` – Stream agent execution events in real-time\n- Environment variables: `LANGSMITH_TRACING=true`, `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (or other provider keys)\n\n## When to use\n\nReach for this skill when:\n- Building an AI agent that calls tools in a loop until a task completes\n- Configuring models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) and tool definitions\n- Adding custom behavior via middleware (retries, summarization, guardrails, human-in-the-loop)\n- Designing complex workflows that mix deterministic and agentic steps\n- Managing agent state, memory, and conversation history across turns\n- Testing, evaluating, and debugging agent behavior\n- Deploying agents to production with observability and persistence\n- Integrating with external services via MCP (Model Context Protocol)\n- Building multi-agent systems with subagents and handoffs\n\n## Quick reference\n\n### Agent creation patterns\n\n| Pattern | Use case | Key parameters |\n|---------|----------|-----------------|\n| `create_agent()` | Simple agent with model, tools, prompt | `model`, `tools`, `system_prompt`, `middleware` |\n| `create_deep_agent()` | Complex tasks with filesystem, memory, subagents | `model`, `tools`, `memory`, `subagents`, `interrupt_on` |\n| `StateGraph` | Custom workflows with nodes and edges | `add_node()`, `add_edge()`, `add_conditional_edges()` |\n\n### Model identifiers\n\n```python\n# String format: \"provider:model\"\n\"openai:gpt-5.5\"\n\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n\"google_genai:gemini-2.5-flash-lite\"\n\"bedrock_converse:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n\n# Or pass initialized model instance\nfrom langchain.chat_models import init_chat_model\nmodel = init_chat_model(\"gpt-5.5\", api_key=\"...\")\n```\n\n### Tool definition\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.tools import tool\n\n@tool\ndef get_weather(city: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get weather for a given city.\"\"\"\n    return f\"It's sunny in {city}!\"\n\n# Or pass any callable with type hints\ndef search_docs(query: str) -> str:\n    return \"search results...\"\n\nagent = create_agent(\n    model=\"gpt-5.5\",\n    tools=[get_weather, search_docs],\n)\n```\n\n### Middleware hooks\n\n| Hook | When it runs | Use case |\n|------|--------------|----------|\n| `before_agent` | Before agent starts | Load memory, validate input |\n| `before_model` | Before each LLM call | Update prompts, trim messages |\n| `wrap_model_call` | Around each LLM call | Intercept requests/responses, dynamic tools |\n| `wrap_tool_call` | Around each tool call | Intercept tool execution, logging |\n| `after_model` | After each LLM response | Validate output, apply guardrails |\n| `after_agent` | After agent completes | Save results, cleanup |\n\n### Invocation patterns\n\n```python\n# Single turn\nresult = agent.invoke({\n    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather?\"}]\n})\n\n# Persistent conversation with thread_id\nresult = agent.invoke(\n    {\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What's the weather?\"}]},\n    config={\"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"user-123\"}}\n)\n\n# With runtime context (user ID, API keys, etc.)\nresult = agent.invoke(\n    {\"messages\": [...]},\n    config={\n        \"configurable\": {\"thread_id\": \"user-123\"},\n        \"context\": {\"user_id\": \"user-123\", \"api_key\": \"...\"}\n    }\n)\n\n# Streaming events\nfor event in agent.stream({\"messages\": [...]}):\n    print(event)\n```\n\n## Decision guidance\n\n### When to use LangChain vs. LangGraph vs. Deep Agents\n\n| Scenario | Use | Why |\n|----------|-----|-----|\n| Simple agent with model + tools + prompt | `create_agent()` | Minimal, configurable harness; compose only what you need |\n| Complex task: filesystem, memory, subagents, planning | `create_deep_agent()` | Batteries-included; built on LangChain and LangGraph |\n| Custom workflow: mix deterministic and agentic steps | `StateGraph` | Low-level control; durable execution, persistence, human-in-the-loop |\n| Need to integrate with existing LangGraph graph | Embed agent as node/subgraph | Middleware travels with the agent; compose freely |\n\n### When to use middleware vs. custom logic\n\n| Concern | Middleware | Custom logic |\n|---------|-----------|--------------|\n| Retries, fallbacks, rate limits | ✓ Use `ModelRetryMiddleware`, `ToolRetryMiddleware` | Only if middleware doesn't fit |\n| Summarization, context compression | ✓ Use `SummarizationMiddleware` | Only for custom compression |\n| Human-in-the-loop approval | ✓ Use `HumanInTheLoopMiddleware` | Only for complex approval flows |\n| PII detection, guardrails | ✓ Use `PIIMiddleware` | Only for custom policies |\n| Dynamic tool selection | ✓ Use `wrap_model_call` hook | Only if tools are unknown at startup |\n| Custom logging, analytics | ✓ Use custom middleware | Preferred for observability |\n\n### When to use tools vs. subagents\n\n| Scenario | Use | Why |\n|----------|-----|-----|\n| Single action: call API, read file, search | Tool | Direct, synchronous, returns result |\n| Complex subtask: multi-step, long-running, parallel | Subagent | Isolated context, autonomous execution, returns final report |\n| Need to parallelize work | Subagent | Subagents run independently; main agent stays focused |\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Building an agent\n\n1. **Define the task and identify tools.** What does the agent need to do? What external actions does it need to take (APIs, databases, file operations)?\n\n2. **Choose a model.** Pick a provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.) and model. Set `PROVIDER_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n3. **Define tools.** Use `@tool` decorator or pass callables with type hints. Include docstrings so the model understands what each tool does.\n\n4. **Create the agent.** Use `create_agent()` for simple cases or `create_deep_agent()` for complex tasks. Pass model, tools, and system prompt.\n\n5. **Add middleware if needed.** For retries, summarization, human-in-the-loop, or custom behavior, pass middleware list to `create_agent()`.\n\n6. **Test locally.** Invoke the agent with test messages. Use `stream()` to see intermediate steps. Check tool calls and responses.\n\n7. **Enable tracing.** Set `LANGSMITH_TRACING=true` and `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` to see traces in LangSmith. Inspect tool calls, state transitions, and latency.\n\n8. **Evaluate quality.** Create a dataset of test cases. Run evaluations in LangSmith to measure accuracy, latency, and cost.\n\n9. **Deploy.** Use LangSmith deployment platform or self-hosted LangGraph server. Configure checkpointer for persistence.\n\n### Customizing agent behavior with middleware\n\n1. **Identify the hook.** Determine when you need to intervene: before model call, after tool execution, etc.\n\n2. **Create middleware.** Use `@create_middleware` or `createMiddleware()` to define hooks.\n\n3. **Implement the hook.** Write logic to intercept, transform, or validate data.\n\n4. **Pass to agent.** Add middleware to `create_agent(..., middleware=[...])`.\n\n5. **Test the behavior.** Invoke the agent and verify the middleware runs at the right time.\n\n### Debugging an agent\n\n1. **Enable tracing.** Set `LANGSMITH_TRACING=true` to capture all steps.\n\n2. **Open LangSmith.** View the trace in the UI. Inspect messages, tool calls, and state.\n\n3. **Check tool outputs.** Did the tool return what you expected? Is the model seeing the right context?\n\n4. **Review the prompt.** Is the system prompt clear? Does the model understand the task?\n\n5. **Inspect state.** Use custom state fields to track intermediate values. Log them in middleware.\n\n6. **Test tools independently.** Call tools directly to verify they work outside the agent loop.\n\n## Common gotchas\n\n- **Missing tool docstrings.** The model uses docstrings to understand what tools do. Always include clear, concise descriptions.\n\n- **Tools that don't return strings.** Tool results must be serializable to strings or message content blocks. Return JSON strings for complex data.\n\n- **Forgetting thread_id for persistence.** Without `thread_id` in config, conversation history is not persisted. Always pass it for multi-turn conversations.\n\n- **Checkpointer not configured.** Agents need a checkpointer to persist state. Use `InMemorySaver()` locally or configure one when deploying.\n\n- **Too many tools.** Passing 20+ tools overwhelms the model's context. Use dynamic tool selection or subagents to reduce the tool list.\n\n- **Middleware order matters.** Middleware runs in the order you pass them. Retries should come before summarization; summarization before human-in-the-loop.\n\n- **Model rate limits.** Production agents hit rate limits. Use `ModelRetryMiddleware` with exponential backoff to handle transient failures.\n\n- **Context window overflow.** Long conversations fill the context window. Use `SummarizationMiddleware` to compress history automatically.\n\n- **Subagent context isolation.** Subagents don't inherit parent agent state. Pass only the data they need via the task description.\n\n- **MCP servers not found.** If using MCP tools, ensure the server is running and reachable. Check connection details in agent logs.\n\n- **Dynamic tools not executing.** When adding tools at runtime via `wrap_model_call`, you must also handle execution in `wrap_tool_call`.\n\n- **Structured output validation.** If using `response_format=`, the model may fail to produce valid JSON. Use a fallback model or retry middleware.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\nBefore submitting an agent to production:\n\n- [ ] All tools have clear docstrings explaining what they do\n- [ ] Tools return serializable data (strings, JSON, or message content blocks)\n- [ ] Agent is configured with a checkpointer for persistence\n- [ ] `thread_id` is passed on every invocation for multi-turn conversations\n- [ ] Tracing is enabled (`LANGSMITH_TRACING=true`) and API key is set\n- [ ] Agent has been tested with representative inputs\n- [ ] Middleware is ordered correctly (retries → summarization → human-in-the-loop)\n- [ ] Tool calls are logged and inspected in LangSmith\n- [ ] Rate limit handling is in place (retry middleware or fallback model)\n- [ ] Context window usage is monitored; summarization is enabled if needed\n- [ ] Human-in-the-loop is configured for high-impact actions (writes, deletes, API calls)\n- [ ] Evaluation dataset exists and quality metrics are tracked\n\n## Resources\n\n**Comprehensive navigation:** https://docs.langchain.com/llms.txt\n\n**Critical pages:**\n- [LangChain overview](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/overview) – Framework architecture and core concepts\n- [Agents guide](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/agents) – Agent creation, invocation, and configuration\n- [Middleware overview](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/middleware/overview) – How middleware works and when hooks fire\n- [LangGraph overview](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/overview) – Low-level orchestration, persistence, and human-in-the-loop\n- [Deep Agents overview](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/overview) – Batteries-included harness with filesystem, memory, and subagents\n- [LangSmith observability](https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/observability) – Tracing, debugging, and monitoring agents\n\n---\n\n> For additional documentation and navigation, see: https://docs.langchain.com/llms.txt"
    },
