        "content": "---\nname: Run Comfy\ndescription: Use when deploying ComfyUI workflows as serverless APIs, running hosted models on-demand, training LoRA models, managing inference deployments, or integrating AI assistants with RunComfy via MCP. Agents should reach for this skill when building production inference pipelines, managing GPU-backed workloads, or automating AI model operations.\nmetadata:\n    mintlify-proj: runcomfy\n    version: \"1.0\"\n---\n\n# RunComfy Skill\n\n## Product summary\n\nRunComfy is a serverless platform for deploying ComfyUI workflows, running hosted models, and training LoRAs. It provides four core APIs (Serverless API for ComfyUI, Serverless API for LoRA, Model API, and Trainer API), a CLI for terminal-based operations, and an MCP server for AI assistant integration. All APIs follow an async queue pattern: submit a job → get a `request_id` → poll status/result or use webhooks. Authentication uses Bearer tokens from your Profile page. Primary docs: https://docs.runcomfy.com\n\n**Key files and endpoints:**\n- API base: `https://api.runcomfy.net/prod/v2/`\n- Model API: `https://model-api.runcomfy.net/v1/`\n- CLI: `runcomfy` command (install via `npx @runcomfy/cli` or `npm i -g @runcomfy/cli`)\n- MCP: `https://mcp.runcomfy.com/mcp`\n- Token storage: `~/.config/runcomfy/token.json` (CLI)\n- Workflow files: `workflow.json` (UI), `workflow_api.json` (API execution), `object_info.json` (schema)\n\n## When to use\n\nReach for this skill when:\n- **Deploying workflows**: turning a cloud-saved ComfyUI workflow into a production API endpoint with configurable hardware and autoscaling\n- **Running models on-demand**: executing hosted models from the catalog without deployment (Model API)\n- **Training LoRAs**: submitting AI Toolkit training jobs with datasets\n- **Managing deployments**: creating, updating, scaling, or deleting serverless endpoints\n- **Polling async jobs**: tracking inference requests, training jobs, or dataset uploads\n- **Integrating AI assistants**: connecting Claude, Cursor, ChatGPT, or other MCP clients to RunComfy\n- **Automating workflows**: using the CLI in scripts, CI/CD, or agent-driven pipelines\n- **Handling media inputs**: passing images/videos to workflows via public URLs or Base64 data URIs\n\n## Quick reference\n\n### Authentication\n```bash\n# CLI: device-code OAuth flow\nruncomfy login\n\n# CI/scripts: set env var\nexport RUNCOMFY_TOKEN=<your-api-key>\n\n# API: Bearer token header\nAuthorization: Bearer <your-api-key>\n```\n\n### Core CLI commands\n| Command | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `runcomfy run <model_id> --input '{...}'` | Run a hosted model end-to-end |\n| `runcomfy deployments list` | List your deployments |\n| `runcomfy deployments run <id> --overrides '{...}'` | Submit inference to a deployment |\n| `runcomfy deployments create --name <N> --workflow-id <UUID> --workflow-version <V>` | Create a new deployment |\n| `runcomfy datasets create --name <N>` | Create a training dataset |\n| `runcomfy train submit --config <PATH> --wait` | Submit a LoRA training job |\n| `runcomfy balance` | Check account balance |\n\n### API endpoints (Serverless API v2)\n| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |\n| --- | :---: | --- |\n| `/prod/v2/deployments/{id}/inference` | POST | Submit inference request |\n| `/prod/v2/deployments/{id}/requests/{req_id}/status` | GET | Poll request status |\n| `/prod/v2/deployments/{id}/requests/{req_id}/result` | GET | Fetch outputs (7-day retention) |\n| `/prod/v2/deployments/{id}/requests/{req_id}/cancel` | POST | Cancel queued/running request |\n| `/prod/v2/deployments/{id}/requests/{req_id}` | DELETE | Purge inputs/outputs immediately |\n\n### Workflow files\n| File | Contains | Use case |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `workflow.json` | Full UI export (nodes, layout, groups) | Editing in ComfyUI UI |\n| `workflow_api.json` | Execution graph only (nodes, inputs, connections) | API calls via `overrides` |\n| `object_info.json` | Node schemas (input types, ranges, defaults) | Validating inputs, building UIs |\n\n### GPU hardware tiers\n| VRAM | Models |\n| --- | --- |\n| 16GB | T4, A4000 |\n| 24GB | A10G, A5000 |\n| 48GB | A6000 |\n| 48GB+ | L40S, L40 |\n| 80GB | A100 |\n| 80GB+ | H100 |\n| 141GB | H200 |\n\n## Decision guidance\n\n### When to use each API\n\n| Scenario | API | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Run a model from the catalog without setup | Model API | No deployment, per-request billing, instant |\n| Deploy your own ComfyUI workflow as an endpoint | Serverless API (ComfyUI) | Stable `deployment_id`, choose hardware, autoscale, webhooks |\n| Run a LoRA without deploying | Model API + LoRA inputs | On-demand, no infrastructure |\n| Serve a LoRA behind a dedicated endpoint | Serverless API (LoRA) | Dedicated hardware, autoscaling, stable endpoint |\n| Train a LoRA from a dataset | Trainer API | Upload dataset, submit config, track progress |\n\n### Polling vs. webhooks\n\n| Approach | Use when | Trade-off |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Polling (`GET .../status`) | Testing, low-volume requests, simple scripts | Higher latency, more API calls |\n| Webhooks (`webhook` field in request) | Production, high volume, real-time updates | Requires public endpoint to receive callbacks |\n\n### Deployment autoscaling\n\n| Setting | Use case | Cost impact |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `min_instances=0, max=1, keep_warm=60` | Bursty traffic, cost-sensitive | Scale-to-zero idle, ~2min cold start |\n| `min_instances=1, max=1, keep_warm=60` | Steady traffic, latency-critical | Always warm, continuous GPU cost |\n| `min_instances=0, max=8, keep_warm=120` | High concurrency, variable load | Scales up on demand, longer keep-warm reduces cold starts |\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Deploying a ComfyUI workflow\n\n1. **Build and test in ComfyUI Cloud**\n   - Open RunComfy, launch a ComfyUI session\n   - Build/modify your workflow, run it end-to-end\n   - Confirm it works before proceeding\n\n2. **Cloud Save the workflow**\n   - Click **Workflow → Cloud Save**\n   - This creates an immutable version with all dependencies\n\n3. **Export workflow files**\n   - Click **Workflow → Export (API)** to get `workflow_api.json`\n   - Click **Workflow → Export** to get `workflow.json` (optional, for reference)\n   - Fetch `object_info.json` from the running instance (Settings → Lite Graph → Node ID Badge Mode: Show All)\n\n4. **Identify node IDs and inputs**\n   - Open `workflow_api.json` in a text editor\n   - Find the node IDs (string keys) you want to override\n   - Note the input names under each node's `inputs` object\n\n5. **Create a deployment**\n   - Go to **Deployments → Deploy workflow as API**\n   - Select your workflow by name or ID\n   - Choose hardware (test in ComfyUI first to estimate VRAM)\n   - Configure autoscaling (start with min=0, max=1, keep_warm=60)\n   - Click **Deploy**, copy the `deployment_id`\n\n6. **Test with an API call**\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST https://api.runcomfy.net/prod/v2/deployments/{deployment_id}/inference \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n       \"overrides\": {\n         \"6\": {\"inputs\": {\"text\": \"your prompt\"}},\n         \"25\": {\"inputs\": {\"noise_seed\": 123456}}\n       }\n     }'\n   ```\n\n7. **Poll for results**\n   ```bash\n   curl https://api.runcomfy.net/prod/v2/deployments/{deployment_id}/requests/{request_id}/status \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\"\n   ```\n\n8. **Fetch outputs** (available for 7 days)\n   ```bash\n   curl https://api.runcomfy.net/prod/v2/deployments/{deployment_id}/requests/{request_id}/result \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\"\n   ```\n\n### Running a hosted model\n\n1. **Find a model**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy models list --search \"flux\" --category \"text-to-image\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Inspect its schema**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy models get blackforestlabs/flux-1-kontext/pro/edit\n   ```\n\n3. **Run it**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy run blackforestlabs/flux-1-kontext/pro/edit \\\n     --input '{\"prompt\": \"a mountain landscape\", \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\"}'\n   ```\n\n4. **Or submit and poll manually**\n   ```bash\n   # Submit\n   curl -X POST https://model-api.runcomfy.net/v1/models/blackforestlabs/flux-1-kontext/pro/edit \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"prompt\": \"...\"}'\n   \n   # Poll\n   curl https://model-api.runcomfy.net/v1/requests/{request_id}/status \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\"\n   ```\n\n### Training a LoRA\n\n1. **Create a dataset**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy datasets create --name my-dataset\n   ```\n\n2. **Upload images and captions**\n   ```bash\n   # Each image needs a .txt caption with the same base name\n   runcomfy datasets upload <dataset_id> ./my-dataset/ --wait\n   ```\n\n3. **Write an AI Toolkit config** (YAML)\n   ```yaml\n   name: my_lora\n   base_model_name: \"model_name\"\n   datasets:\n     - folder_path: \"/app/ai-toolkit/datasets/my-dataset\"\n   training_folder: \"/app/ai-toolkit/output\"\n   # ... other settings\n   ```\n\n4. **Submit training**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy train submit --config ./config.yaml --wait\n   ```\n\n5. **Monitor progress**\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy train status <job_id>\n   ```\n\n6. **Fetch results** (checkpoints, samples)\n   ```bash\n   runcomfy train result <job_id> --download\n   ```\n\n## Common gotchas\n\n- **API v1 is deprecated**: Always use `/prod/v2/` endpoints. v1 will be retired.\n- **Overrides must match `workflow_api.json`**: Node IDs and input names are case-sensitive. Use the exact keys from the exported file.\n- **Results expire after 7 days**: Download or copy outputs to your own storage if you need long-term retention.\n- **Cold starts on scale-to-zero**: Setting `min_instances=0` saves cost but first request after idle takes ~2 minutes. Use `min_instances=1` for latency-critical apps.\n- **Media inputs require public URLs or Base64**: Local file paths, share links, or expired presigned URLs will fail with `FileUploadException`. Use direct HTTPS URLs or `data:` URIs.\n- **Workflow versions are immutable**: Creating a new Cloud Save doesn't update running deployments. Explicitly update the deployment to use the new version.\n- **Node ID display**: Enable **Settings → Lite Graph → Node ID Badge Mode: Show All** in ComfyUI to see node IDs on the canvas.\n- **Ctrl-C cancels remote jobs**: The CLI auto-cancels when you interrupt. If the cancel fails, it prints the `request_id` so you can retry.\n- **Polling vs. webhooks**: Polling is simpler for testing but scales poorly. Use webhooks in production.\n- **GPU out-of-memory**: If a run fails with OOM, reduce resolution/batch/steps or upgrade to a larger GPU tier.\n- **No new outputs on identical runs**: ComfyUI caches results. Change the seed or any input to force a new output.\n- **Deployment disabled on insufficient funds**: If your balance is too low, the deployment auto-disables. Add funds and re-enable it.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\nBefore submitting work with RunComfy:\n\n- [ ] API token is valid and not expired (regenerate from Profile if needed)\n- [ ] Deployment exists and is enabled (check `runcomfy deployments list`)\n- [ ] Workflow has been Cloud Saved and a version exists\n- [ ] `workflow_api.json` has been exported and node IDs are correct\n- [ ] Overrides match the deployed workflow (node IDs and input names are exact)\n- [ ] Media inputs are public HTTPS URLs or valid Base64 data URIs (not local paths)\n- [ ] GPU hardware tier has enough VRAM for your workflow (test in ComfyUI first)\n- [ ] Autoscaling settings match your traffic pattern (min/max instances, keep-warm)\n- [ ] Request body is valid JSON and matches the API schema\n- [ ] Bearer token is included in `Authorization` header\n- [ ] For CLI: `RUNCOMFY_TOKEN` env var is set or `runcomfy login` has been run\n- [ ] Results are downloaded/saved before 7-day expiration\n- [ ] Webhooks are configured if polling is not feasible\n- [ ] Error responses include `error_code` and `message` for debugging\n\n## Resources\n\n**Comprehensive navigation**: https://docs.runcomfy.com/llms.txt\n\n**Critical documentation pages**:\n- [Serverless API (ComfyUI) Introduction](https://docs.runcomfy.com/serverless/introduction) — core concepts, deployment lifecycle\n- [Async Queue Endpoints](https://docs.runcomfy.com/serverless/async-queue-endpoints) — submit, poll, cancel, delete requests\n- [Workflow Files](https://docs.runcomfy.com/serverless/workflow-files) — understand `workflow_api.json`, `object_info.json`, overrides\n- [CLI Commands](https://docs.runcomfy.com/cli/commands) — full reference for `runcomfy` CLI\n- [Error Codes](https://docs.runcomfy.com/serverless/error-codes) — troubleshoot API failures\n- [Model API Quickstart](https://docs.runcomfy.com/model-apis/quickstart) — run hosted models without deployment\n- [MCP Introduction](https://docs.runcomfy.com/mcp/introduction) — integrate AI assistants\n\n---\n\n> For additional documentation and navigation, see: https://docs.runcomfy.com/llms.txt"
